.TH MBUS-CTL 8
.SH NAME
mbus-ctl \- monitor and control the MODBUS gateway
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mbus-ctl SHOW
.RB { CONNECTIONS | LINES | GATEWAY }
.RI [ /CONTINUOUS [ =seconds ]]
.br
.B mbus-ctl RESET CONNECTIONS
.RI { id | address | address:port | /ALL }
.br
.B mbus-ctl RESTART GATEWAY
.RI [ /WAIT= seconds " | " /NOWAIT ]
.br
.B mbus-ctl HELP
.SH DESCRIPTION
Communicate with a running mbusgw-t2r gateway through its local control socket.
SHOW displays clients, serial lines or gateway status.
RESET disconnects selected clients.
RESTART validates the settings and restarts the running gateway.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI /SOCKET= path
Connect to
.I path
instead of /var/run/mbusgw-t2r.sock.
.TP
.RI /CONTINUOUS[ =seconds ]
Refresh SHOW output until interrupted.
.TP
.BI /WAIT= seconds
Wait for the gateway to restart.
.TP
.B /NOWAIT
Do not wait for the gateway to restart.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mbusgw-t2r (8)
